    "label": "thm:lb-AS-logT",
    "number": "Theorem 3",
    "quote": "There exist universal constants $d_0, d_1 > 0$ such that the following holds. For any constant $C \\geq 1$, if an anytime algorithm $\\mathcal{A}$ achieves expected regret at most $d_0 \\sqrt{NT} (\\ln (NT))^{C}$ for all $T$ and all instances with $N$ items, then for any $N \\geq 2$, $T_0 \\geq N$ ... there exists an instance with $N$ items and a time horizon $T \\in [T_0, T_0^2]$, such that the expected number of assortment switches before time $T$ is at least $d_1 N \\log T / (C \\log \\log (NT))$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Lower bound on expected assortment switches; hard instance uses capacity K=1."
  },
